A||N||17||FieroJoe||Rodney's Short Shifter: Pro & Con?||||5||
Z||000000||FieroJoe||02-11-2001||08:57 PM||||Anybody have Rodney's OEM short shifter installed on thier Fiero?  I was thinking about getting his, you get a lot more for the money as compared to the Fiero Store, and there is no core charge.  How much different is it shifting?  Better feel?  Anybody have pics of it installed?<P>Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Formula88||02-11-2001||09:33 PM||||Don't know about Rodney's shifter, but if you're looking for value, how about free?  The shifter in the 87-88 with the dogleg bend instead of the sharp L bend...just cut the handle off below the last bend before it goes into the shift knob.  Yes, the knob is now at a slight angle, but it angles directly into your hand.  And the shorter length makes is feel great.  And you don't even have to remove the shifter, although it might be easier if you did.  Haven't done it to mine, yet, but LZeitgeist has done it to the last two of his Fieros and it looks and feels great.<P>------------------<BR>We all come into this world the same way; naked, screaming, and covered in blood.  If you're lucky, it doesn't have to end there.||||reg||6
Z||000002||Bob Englert||02-11-2001||09:49 PM||||I have had Rodney's Short Shifter (not the OEM version) in 3 different cars.  I love how it feels.  I wouldn't own a manual Fiero without one!<P>Highly recommended...<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000003||TwisT||02-11-2001||10:09 PM||||Ok,  again,  not a owner of Rodney's shifter...  but I've had experience in doing it myself.  I shortened my '88's simply by removing the shifter,  cutting out the curved section of the rod,  and rewelding the two pieces together.  It's been a while,  but I think it took out about 2 1/2" or so.  Very slick and works like a charm...  and CHEAP!  (cost nothing)<P>If you don't have a welder,  just cut the rod and bring it to a shop to have it done.  Piece of cake.<P>Brett||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroWife||02-11-2001||10:11 PM||||We have one on our 87 Coupe... I'm not sure where it came from, 87ECO5 will have to fill in that blank, but I think it's great.  It shifts very smoothly and it's easier to handle.  I'm kind of short, 5'4", and it's much easier for me to shift.  Just my $.02...<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/fierowife/Signature.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000005||Monkeyman||02-11-2001||10:25 PM||||I've got Rodneys supershort shifter.  I like it alot.  Much better than the original, IMO.  I think I paid somewhere around $75US.  Is it worth it?  It was to me.  If you're good at welding/cutting/fabrication, you could do it yourself for less.  On the other hand, this took all of about 5 minutes to install and I didn't even have to get dirty or break a sweat.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ronnie||02-11-2001||11:06 PM||||OK, I don't have Rodney's either. But I installed a shifter from a 84-85 Fiero in both of my cars.They are 1.5 inches shorter than the 86-87 shifters.Looks alot better and shifts crisper than the (rowboat) shifter did. Took no more than 10 mins to install and NO cutting or welding.I have a spare I'll sell you for $10 bucks plus shipping and handling.Also can keep the original shift boot with no alteration.<P>------------------<BR>Black '86GT 4spd / Silver '87GT 5spd<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BOTHGTS_1.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000007||Neverfinished||02-11-2001||11:23 PM||||This is exactly what I did. I found this page after i figured this out on my own. I recommend it alot. <A HREF="http://fierozone.tripod.com/weekend/shifter/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://fierozone.tripod.com/weekend/shifter/index.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||2xsess||02-12-2001||07:18 AM||||I have one of FieroDave's short shifters in my car. At first it was wierd but now I'd never have another manual Fiero without one.<P>Pics on my website. I think there are even some before and after shots.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2xsess.gif">      <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>Visit My Website</A>||||reg||1
Z||000009||FieroJoe||02-12-2001||07:47 AM||||Thanks all, I might have to try that with cutting, welding, and re-threading it.  I am good with a MIG and arc welding, so I think I could handle it.<P>Thanks again!<P>||||reg||1
